00:05:31.000 --> 00:06:01.000
You'll do a pretty good job picturing it if you imagine the new logo as the old logo, but a talusized. Changing an ISO standard isn't easy. A proposal has to be submitted and reviewed by ISO's Technical Committee on Graphical Symbols. Then it has to be considered by symbols experts from around the world and then finally approved by ISO's member countries. I talked with Barry Gray, the chairman of the Technical Committee on Graphical Symbols. Oh my God, I want Barry Gray's job.
如果你把新标志想象成旧标志的斜体版，你就能很好地描绘出它的样子。改变ISO标准并不容易。必须提交提案并由ISO图形符号技术委员会进行审查。然后必须由来自世界各地的符号专家进行审议，最后由ISO成员国批准。我采访了图形符号技术委员会主席巴里·格雷。天哪，我想做巴里·格雷的工作。

