there are still questions about what constitutes a functional equivalent. New York City had planned to adopt the new logo in all five burrows, but this legal ambiguity caused them to hold off implementing it, at least for now. I think a lot of people end up buying that old original image because they're nervous about complying with ADA code. And I think what we're trying to do is say, look, functional equivalence has a kind of legal set of definitions and contours. Those are the things that are going to probably need to be worked out at the state level.
